# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# generated at build time by scripts/copy-maplibre-worker.mjs
#
# MapLibre cannot derive its worker URL once bundled (import.meta.url is not an
# http URL, so new Worker("") resolves to "/" and the browser is served HTML).
# The worker is copied into public/ verbatim at build time and MapView points at
# it with setWorkerUrl(). Committing a vendored 500 kB library bundle would mean
# tracking a file that changes on every maplibre-gl upgrade.
public/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs
public/maplibre-gl-shared.mjs

# The satellite pass worker, bundled by scripts/build-passes-worker.mjs. Same
# reasoning as the MapLibre worker above - it is build output, not source. Unlike
# the MapLibre one it is not 500 kB of vendored library, but it is regenerated by
# `npm run build` (which runs before `next build`), so there is nothing to commit.
public/passes-worker.mjs

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# generated data layers - NOW COMMITTED
#
# The ingest output is committed on purpose. This deploy is a static export to
# Cloudflare Pages, and static hosting serves files: there is no build step on
# the far side that could run `npm run ingest:all` for us, and no long-lived
# process that could produce the data on first request. Either the data is in
# the repository or the deployed map has 39 empty layers and says nothing about
# why, because the registry still lists every one of them.
#
# The ~10 MB of churn that motivated gitignoring this is now unavoidable rather
# than merely annoying: an ingest run that changes nothing material still
# rewrites the manifest timestamp. Refresh it deliberately
# (`npm run ingest:all && git add public/data`), not incidentally.
#
# Several layers are MANNGIS-derived and redistributed under OGL-derived terms.
# Committing them is a licensing decision that has now been taken; see
# DEPLOY.md and src/lib/sources.ts for the per-layer terms.
#
# The ingest scripts stay in the repo and stay runnable. Regenerating is still
# the documented path for refreshing the data, it is just no longer the only way
# to obtain it.
#
# public/data/
# stray editor/agent backups
*.bak
